The code statements that lead to the bug are:
ret = hfi_ops->session_release_buf(inst, buffer);
buffer->attr |= BUF_ATTR_PENDING_RELEASE;
Reason:
The call `session_release_buf()` may free the buffer. The subsequent assignment to `buffer->attr` accesses freed memory, causing a use-after-free condition.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
buffer->attr |= BUF_ATTR_PENDING_RELEASE;
ret = hfi_ops->session_release_buf(inst, buffer);
if (ret) {
    buffer->attr &= ~BUF_ATTR_PENDING_RELEASE;
    return ret;
}
Reason:
Setting the flag before the call ensures that if `session_release_buf()` frees the buffer, no further access to `buffer` occurs. The flag revert only happens if the call returns an error (i.e., the buffer was not freed), which is safe.

